Long shift.
Cold cup.
“Have you tried
Turning it off?”

Came home with a pounding head,
Server fans still in my ears.
Someone called a printer jam
“The worst outage in years.”
Caroline was heating dinner.
I had cleared a space for me.
Said, “What’s that you’re installing?”
I said, “Oh-Mah-Chee.”
It was ready before dinner.
Then I thought, “Let’s make it mine.”
She said, “So now you’re finished?”
“Installed? Yeah. Works just fine.”

Just five more minutes.
Five more minutes!
Then I’m going to bed.
Got a terminal wide open
And a little plan in my head.
Kept their systems up all day,
Got some things of my own to do.
Let me change this one last setting—
And it’s half past two.

Super and Return,
And a shell appeared on cue.
Got my windows neatly tiled,
Picked a shade of midnight blue.

Just five more minutes.
Five more minutes!
Then I’m going to bed.
Got a terminal wide open
And a little plan in my head.
Kept their systems up all day,
Got some things of my own to do.
Let me change this one last setting—
And it’s half past two.

Super and Return,
And a shell appeared on cue.
Got my windows neatly tiled,
Picked a shade of midnight blue.
Caroline slid dinner over.
I slid over to make room.
Said, “I’m nearly done here, honey.”
She said, “Then pick up your spoon.”
Pushed my dot files up to GitHub,
Said, “That ought to stick.”
Took a bite and eyed the borders.
Just a little bit too thick.

So I changed a little binding,
Moved a window, changed it back.
Made the letters slightly bigger,
Made the borders almost black.
“Wasn’t blue the one you wanted?”
“Yes, but look how clean this feels.”
She said, “Shame you can’t use shortcuts
To reheat these poor old meals.”

“Five more minutes.”

Found a line inside my config,
Thought I’d give that tweak a try.
Saved the change and saw my windows
Spread a little bit too wide.
Caroline stood in the doorway:
“Got a copy of that bit?”
I said, “Pushed it up to GitHub.”

“For once, I thought of it.”

Brought it back to how I had it.
She said, “Great. Now let it sit.”

Just five more minutes.

Just five more minutes.
Five more minutes!
Then I’m going to bed.
Got a terminal wide open
And a little plan in my head.
Kept their systems up all day,
Got some things of my own to do.
Let me change this one last setting—
And it’s half past two.

She came down to make the coffee.
I was sitting in her chair.
Morning light across the table,
Little windows everywhere.

Just five more minutes.
Five more minutes!
Then I’m going to bed.
Got a terminal wide open
And a little plan in my head.
Kept their systems up all day,
Got some things of my own to do.
Let me change this one last setting—
And it’s half past two.

She came down to make the coffee.
I was sitting in her chair.
Morning light across the table,
Little windows everywhere.
Said, “Well, show me what you’ve done.”
So I took her through the keys.
Opened this and shifted that.
She said, “That does look neat.”
Then she pointed to the center:
“Does that clock say six fifteen?”

I said, “Want a different format?”
She said, “You know what I mean.”

Just five more minutes.
Five more minutes!
She said, “Here we go.”
Got a terminal wide open
And the coffee getting low.
Then she leaned across the table:
“Could you make that green, not blue?”
Now she’s scrolling through the colors.
Now I’m pulling chairs for two.
Five more minutes!
“Try the darker one in there.”
Five more minutes!
Now she’s settled in my chair.

She said,
“Can you put Oh-Mah-Chee on mine?”
Then she pointed to the center:
“Does that clock say six fifteen?”

I said, “Want a different format?”
She said, “You know what I mean.”

Just five more minutes.
Five more minutes!
She said, “Here we go.”
Got a terminal wide open
And the coffee getting low.
Then she leaned across the table:
“Could you make that green, not blue?”
Now she’s scrolling through the colors.
Now I’m pulling chairs for two.
Five more minutes!
“Try the darker one in there.”
Five more minutes!
Now she’s settled in my chair.

She said,
“Can you put Oh-Mah-Chee on mine?”
“Sure. Before the toast is done.”
“And then?”

“Well… what color do you like?”
